  "limitations": [
    "One blind collection on one wall; the millimetre figures are a single sample, not a distribution, so no threshold is frozen.",
    "Pixels outside the inspection region are not required to be covered. That is a choice of acceptance domain, not a claim that they could not be photographed; the envelope split says how many of them a permitted pose could still have reached.",
    "The observable envelope is an upper bound: it grows the frozen coverage_region rather than the maneuver-inset route the planner actually drives, and it counts both sweep axes for both tasks.",
    "The envelope split is bounded by construction on this data. The mosaic domain (x 0.2286..9.7709, y 0.3634..7.6347 m) lies wholly inside the sweep envelope, because it is the union of the frames actually taken and those came from poses the task permitted, so the outside-envelope count can only be zero here. What the split does establish is that not one of the 439,116 excused pixels is excused by reach: every one is a pixel some permitted pose could have photographed, and the excuse rests entirely on the choice of acceptance domain. The count becomes informative only for a run whose mosaic domain reaches past the envelope.",
    "Absolute values from before commit 3f422f5 are not comparable: the photographed surface stood 1.25 mm proud of the drive plane and scaled every mosaic by +4566 ppm.",
    "One horizontal frame carries no accepted match edge because SIFT finds no keypoints on it, so its pose comes from odometry. The measured effect on the nearest anchor is 0.022 mm.",
    "The inspection stage ran at commit 9c89dda and the stages before it at 7f8b875; both trees were clean and the difference is recorded per stage rather than averaged into one claim."
  ],
